From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominik Krivohlavek <github@xkrivo.net>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:18:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/31] fix(midea): report J15 work status 3 as paused instead
 of docked

The firmware sends work status 3 for GoingHomePause and as the fallback
for internal states it has no IoT code for. Showing that as DOCKED hid
a robot paused on its way home and made it non-resumable. Map it to
PAUSED with the resumable flag. Docked detection is unaffected: the
real on-station state is 18, which still maps to DOCKED.

Based on static analysis of the status encoder tables; untested on the
robot.

diff --git a/backend/lib/robots/midea/MideaValetudoRobot.js b/backend/lib/robots/midea/MideaValetudoRobot.js
index 5e143026..1c23a141 100644
--- a/backend/lib/robots/midea/MideaValetudoRobot.js
+++ b/backend/lib/robots/midea/MideaValetudoRobot.js
@@ -1399,8 +1399,9 @@ MideaValetudoRobot.STATUS_MAP = Object.freeze({
     2: {
         value: stateAttrs.StatusStateAttribute.VALUE.DOCKED
     },
-    3: {
-        value: stateAttrs.StatusStateAttribute.VALUE.DOCKED
+    3: { // GoingHomePause, also what the firmware sends for states it can't encode
+        value: stateAttrs.StatusStateAttribute.VALUE.PAUSED,
+        flag: stateAttrs.StatusStateAttribute.FLAG.RESUMABLE
     },
     4: {
         value: stateAttrs.StatusStateAttribute.VALUE.DOCKED
